                <pb facs="0143" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg23"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Jackson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-07-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78. Servian series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report the receipt
                    to-day of a note from Mr. Zujovic, the Servian minister of foreign affairs,
                    requesting the transmission to my government of the expression of the sincere
                    regrets of the Royal Servian Government at the loss suffered by the people of
                    the United States in the person of that very distinguished citizen and eminent
                    statesman Hon. John Hay.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
